.TH WEBKIT-TOOL 1
.SH NAME
webkit-tool \\- statically flag risky WebKit configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webkit-tool
webkit-tool [--scan DIRECTORY]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects a source tree for risky WebKit settings and native script bridges without executing code.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBwebkit-tool --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
